  "rules-note": "Business strikes only: proofs and the 1976 pattern are skipped, and collector-only strikes are dropped (the Satin finish Special Mint Set rows of 1964-1967 and the 1976 S silver-clad uncirculated coins sold only in sets). Mint marks follow the source's Mint cell: a Mint cell in parentheses means the coin has no mark (null), a plain letter is the mark. Mintages come only from the saved source; nothing is summed or estimated. Comments such as \"Doubled die errors are known\" have no separate row or figure and add no variety. No cited source names key dates (not even 1932-D and 1932-S), so isKeyDate is false for every coin. This file holds the copper-nickel clad quarters of 1965-1998; the 90% silver quarters are in us-quarters-washington-silver.json, and the 1999 and later quarters in the other us-quarters-*.json files. 1965-1967 are one no-mark coin each (null) with the (P) figure; the (D) and (S) rows are \"^\" (included above) and add nothing. 1968-1979: a no-mark (P) coin and D; the 1977-1979 (W) rows are \"^\" (included above) and are dropped, including the generator's 1977 note-variety \"First time West Point produced the quarter\". The dual-dated Bicentennial quarters (dated 1776-1976, struck in 1975 and 1976) are year 1976 with variety \"Bicentennial\", no-mark and D; there are no 1975 quarters. P marks appear from 1980: 1980-1998 are P and D.",
